    "body": "Found while auditing #36628 \r\n\r\nAlready known upstream issue with C-tor: https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/core/tor/-/issues/32314\r\n\r\nWith `-proxy` pointed at Tor, outbound connections to IPv6 peers whose\r\n address contains an inner `::` always fail with \"general failure\".\r\n\r\n Core sends every SOCKS5 destination as a DOMAINNAME, with IPv6 in its\r\n compressed form. Tor copies the name into its relay BEGIN cell as\r\n `<name>:<port>`, and the exit's `tor_addr_port_split` first tries to parse\r\n the whole string as an IPv6 address. `2001:db8::1:8333` is a valid one,\r\n because the `::` absorbs the port as an eighth group. The exit then sees no\r\n port and closes the stream. Addresses written with all eight groups, or\r\n ending in `::`, are unaffected: appending `:port` to them does not give a\r\n valid address.\r\n\r\n About 20% of the IPv6 addresses in a gossip-filled addrman, and 29% of\r\n current IPv6 DNS seed answers, have an inner `::`. The failure is closed;\r\n there is no fallback to a direct connection.\r\n\r\n Note that this also effects private broadcast by default.\r\n\r\n This PR sends such addresses with all eight groups written out\r\n (`2001:db8:0:0:0:0:0:1`). `<name>:<port>` then has nine groups, so the exit\r\n splits at the last colon. Other forms:\r\n\r\n | Form                  | Tor         | Tor, SafeSocks 1 | getaddrinfo-based proxies |\r\n |-----------------------|-------------|------------------|---------------------------|\r\n | `2001:db8::1` (today) | fails       | fails            | works                     |\r\n | `[2001:db8::1]`       | works       | works            | fails                     |\r\n | ATYP IPv6             | works, logs a DNS-leak warning | refused | works         |\r\n | eight groups (this PR)| works       | works            | works                     |\r\n\r\n Tested against tor 0.4.9.13: on mainnet, master could not reach four\r\n seed-provided peers with inner-`::` addresses (30 \"general failure\"); with\r\n this change all four connected and completed the version handshake.\r\n `feature_proxy.py` and a new `netbase_tests` case check the bytes sent.",
