      "updated_at": "2026-10-27T14:55:28Z",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Workaround seems fine to do. But it's surprising the Tor daemon does not follow [its own spec](https://torspec-b24541.pages.torproject.net/tor-spec/opening-streams.html) and format the IPv6 with brackets.\r\n\r\nEDIT: had bot lookup the Tor sources and even the [latest version still formats](https://tpo.pages.torproject.net/core/doc/tor/connection__edge_8c_source.html#l03448) IPv6:port ambiguously, contrary to the spec. Arti [does implement](https://tpo.pages.torproject.net/core/doc/rust/private/src/tor_cell/relaycell/msg.rs.html#285) the spec correctly. May be worth upstreaming a bug report.",
      "user": {
