          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/2b5b6fe231ff45a09d9e24411e4420d51ed45cab"
        }
      ],
      "message": "netbase: send shortened IPv6 addresses to SOCKS5 proxies in full\n\nTor copies a SOCKS5 DOMAINNAME into its relay BEGIN cell as\n\"<name>:<port>\", and an exit parses \"2001:db8::1:8333\" as an IPv6\naddress with no port and closes the stream. Outbound connections\nthrough a Tor -proxy to IPv6 addresses that contain \"::\" therefore fail\nwith \"general failure\". About a third of the IPv6 addresses the DNS\nseeds return have this form.\n\nWrite such addresses with all eight groups. \"<name>:<port>\" is then not\nan IPv6 address, so the exit splits it at the last colon, and the name\nis still an address to proxies that resolve it with getaddrinfo, which\nbrackets would break.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Greg Sanders",
        "email": "gsanders87@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-27T14:50:41Z"
      },
